  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.887pt, 387.82pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.887pt, 410.31pt, "Nanoconfined liquid crystals (LCs) and their nanocomposites are driving the next generation of ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 424.85pt, "photonic applications. Consequently, deepening our understanding of mesophase stability, defect ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 439.38pt, "topology, and the dynamic response of LCs at the nanoscale requires the development of novel ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 453.94pt, "characterization approaches.  This motivates us to perform in situ observations on model 4′-octyl-4-")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 468.48pt, "cyanobiphenyl (8CB) LC using liquid-phase scanning transmission electron microscopy (LP-STEM). We ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 482.79pt, "find that the electron beam induced consecutive phase changes from smectic A to nematic (SmA-N) ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 497.32pt, "and from nematic to isotropic (N-I). The kinetic dependence of the phase transition on dose rate shows ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 511.86pt, "that the time between SmA-N and N-I shortens with increasing rate, revealing the hypothesis that a ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 526.4pt, "higher electron dose rate increases the energy dissipation rate, leading to substantial heat generation ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 540.96pt, "in the sample. We report on the spontaneous formation of disclinations, ordering effects, and complete ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 555.26pt, "process reversibility. Radiolytic effects of the electron beam are discussed in detail, and additional ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 569.8pt, "experiments with external heating indicate that the observed phenomena are mainly thermal in ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 584.34pt, "nature. The results are supported by calculations of heat diffusion, suggesting the nanoconfined 8CB ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 598.87pt, "differs significantly in thermal properties compared to the bulk one. This is the first detailed study of ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 613.41pt, "LC phase transitions using LP-STEM, which paves the way for further studies of nanoconfined LCs and ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 627.74pt, "for the development of the technique for advanced LC materials research. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12.038pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.887pt, 673.85pt, "Introduction ")
