  #line-at(70.887pt, 396.46pt, "sandwiched sample in Fig. S1, and more preparation details in Methods. This preparation method does ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 410.99pt, "not ensure uniform LC thickness or full isolation from the vacuum throughout the sample, and this ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 425.53pt, "should be considered when estimating temperature changes associated with specific phase transitions. ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 440.06pt, "In the high vacuum environment the phase change temperatures of the LC sample may be shifted, and ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 454.62pt, "these conditions are in any case far from the standard LC application. Moreover, the LC needs to be ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 468.93pt, "enclosed on both sides to achieve a thin layer. Having the same support on top and bottom provides ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 483.47pt, "uniform effects on the thin film sample, which is crucial for correlating two-dimensional STEM imaging ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 498.01pt, "with the actual three-dimensional structure. The thickness of a typical observation area was 20-40 nm, ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 512.54pt, "estimated using the method described in Supplementary Information (Fig. S3 and S4).For such a low ")
