  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(182.91pt, 364.64pt, "s the phase changes were the most clearly visible among all the dose rate ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 379.19pt, "experiments and the N-I transition appeared at the shortest time, e.g. 32 s in Fig. 1f.  This indicates that ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 393.73pt, "the time needed for the temperature increase to reach N-I transition temperature is increases with the ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 408.27pt, "dose rate value. On the other hand, the onset of the SmA-N transition (Fig. 1f) does not strongly depend ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 422.8pt, "on the dose rate value but to a certain extent on the irradiation time. The difference in SmA-N start ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 437.11pt, "time can be attributed to superheating at higher electron doses  . The highest electron dose rate   heats ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 451.67pt, "more quickly, so the nucleation of the new phase is shifted for higher temperatures. This results in a ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 466.21pt, "slight retardation of SmA-N occurrence in time with increasing electron dose rates. ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 488.69pt, "This hypothesis is consistent with the observation that in uniform areas (Fig. 2) defects did not assist ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 503.23pt, "phase changes. The fact that the N-I transition begins in the center of the observation area (Fig. 2c) is ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 517.77pt, "linked to the geometry of heat dissipation in the sample")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 7.041pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(327.86pt, 514.36pt, "62")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(335.13pt, 517.77pt, ". It is known that when an electron beam ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 532.07pt, "transmits through a thin liquid sample, the electron dose distribution is uniform along the Z-axis (i.e., ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 546.63pt, "through the sample thickness)")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 7.041pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(206.53pt, 543.23pt, "64")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(213.8pt, 546.63pt, ". If we therefore consider temperature variations in this dimension to ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 561.17pt, "be negligible, as they are much smaller than the threshold for phase change, then the heat transfer ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 575.71pt, "takes place primarily in lateral directions (X-Y plane) to regions outside the irradiated area, implying ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 590.24pt, "that the temperature increase will be the highest in the center of the observation area")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 7.041pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(457.14pt, 586.84pt, "62")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(464.41pt, 590.24pt, ". This process ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 604.55pt, "will also be shown and discussed in the next part of this article.  ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.887pt, 627.06pt, "Heat diffusion ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.887pt, 649.55pt, "In order to better understand the thermal processes taking place in 8CB under the influence of an ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 664.08pt, "electron beam, we developed a simulation model corresponding to the observed situation, simplified ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 678.62pt, "to a 1D system. It should be noted that thermal simulations for liquid crystal systems do not yield ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 693.15pt, "consistent results, but only demonstrate the nature of thermal diffusion without fully accounting for ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 707.71pt, "the specific characteristics of liquid crystals. This is because the thermal parameters of planar and ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 722.02pt, "homeotropic alignments of liquid crystals depend on the spatial alignment. In our case, the thin liquid-")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 736.56pt, "crystal layer 8CB consists of a finite number of molecules forming a physicochemical system. The local ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 751.096pt, "addition of heat not only affects the temperature distribution of the entire system, but also influences ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 765.632pt, "the degree of packing and molecular reorientation. Hence, any numerical description using heat ")
]

