  #line-at(70.887pt, 620.25pt, "The specific heat capacity of 8CB is approximately half that of water (4189.9 J/kg·K), meaning it requires ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 634.56pt, "significantly less energy to heat. Furthermore, the thermal diffusivity ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.17pt, 634.56pt, "𝛼")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(384.21pt, 634.56pt, " of 8CB is highly anisotropic and ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 649.09pt, "temperature-dependent, as presented in Table S1. At room temperature, its value (~0.0012 cm²/s) is ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 663.63pt, "close to that of water (0.00143 cm²/s). However, during heating and phase transitions, the thermal ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 678.16pt, "diffusivity of 8CB can drop to 0.0006 cm²/s or even lower. This combination of a low specific heat ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 692.7pt, "capacity and a variable, often low, thermal diffusivity leads to a maximum temperature rise in 8CB that ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 707.03pt, "can be 2.5 to 5 times higher than in water in the same imaging conditions. However, the mechanism ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 721.57pt, "by which energy is delivered to 8CB and water is very likely significantly different, as evidenced by the ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 736.11pt, "poor agreement between the simulation and the experiment, particularly regarding heat distribution ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 750.641pt, "within the sample. This discrepancy between simulation and experiment allows us to hypothesize that ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 765.178pt, "either the thermal properties of 8CB at the sub-microscale differ significantly from their macroscopic ")
]

