  #line-at(349.01pt, 95.87pt, ". Therefore, in the presence of e-beam ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 110.41pt, "electric field,  we propose that the LC molecules align planarly, i.e., in the plane of the sample.  In case ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 124.74pt, "of such subtle contrast variations in low-density")
  #line-at(291.75pt, 124.74pt, "LC sample, we suggest that some stronger inelastic ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 139.28pt, "electron scattering on planarly oriented 8CB molecules may contribute to the darker contrast ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 153.81pt, "appearance for the N phase, similarly to some polymers containing aromatic systems observed in ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 168.35pt, "energy-filtered TEM")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 7.041pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(159.06pt, 164.94pt, "97–99")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(177pt, 168.35pt, ". Additionally, this less organized molecule distribution and librational motions ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 182.89pt, "could result in slight thickness changes on the molecular level.  There is no doubt, however, that this ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 197.2pt, "topic requires more detailed analysis.  ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12.038pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.887pt, 220.84pt, "Conclusions ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.887pt, 243.55pt, "In summary, the novelty of this work lies in the detailed in-situ imaging of electron beam-induced SmA-")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 258.09pt, "N and N-I   phase changes dynamics, together with the defect formation and accompanying surface ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 272.62pt, "phenomena. The hypothesis of a distinctive N phase contrast origin is discussed, emphasizing N phase ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 287.18pt, "reorientation in the beam's electric field and electron interactions with planarly oriented biphenyl rings ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 301.49pt, "of 8CB molecules, which causes higher electron scattering of this phase. By developing a novel laser-")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 316.03pt, "illumination system in TEM, we show the observed phase transitions are predominantly driven by ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 330.57pt, "temperature increase, as they occurred during both electron beam irradiation and with the laser as an ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 345.1pt, "additional heating source. The calculations show that the nanoconfined 8CB differs in thermal ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 359.64pt, "properties significantly compared to the bulk. The phase changes were fully reversible once the heating ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 373.97pt, "source was removed, which suggests not only the temperature-dependent nature of the phenomena, ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 388.51pt, "but also excludes irreversible electron beam damage during the imaging. However, the radiolytic effects ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 403.04pt, "should be studied in more detail, as ion formation could affect sample heating.  ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 425.53pt, "Our work lays a foundation for further in-situ LP-(S)TEM studies of liquid-crystalline materials, including ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 440.06pt, "their advanced nanocomposites. TEM can be used as a powerful device for studying LC response to ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 454.62pt, "electric and magnetic fields, other phase transitions dynamics, nanomaterials assembly in the LC ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 468.93pt, "matrix, or their general interaction with electrons for fundamental knowledge. The application of laser-")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 483.47pt, "induced heating in the TEM offers a pathway for exploring reaction mechanisms and radiolysis effects. ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 498.01pt, "We also see promising prospects for the possibility of controlling LC phase transitions with electron ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 512.54pt, "beam at the sub-micro and nano scale, providing an opportunity to design optical systems with unique ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 527.08pt, "properties. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12.038pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.887pt, 550.72pt, "Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
