  #line-at(70.887pt, 437.11pt, "1–4 is 10, while video 5 has a frame rate of 25. The supplementary video for Fig. 1d (the lowest electron ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 451.67pt, "dose rate of 0.25 e")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 7.041pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(157.7pt, 448.24pt, "-")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(159.74pt, 451.67pt, "/nm")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 7.041pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(178.59pt, 448.24pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(182.23pt, 451.67pt, "s) is not provided because the process was slow, and the individual images ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 466.21pt, "were taken instead of a series.  Image analysis was performed using Velox (ThermoFisher Scientific) ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 480.74pt, "and Fiji software")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 7.041pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(145.41pt, 477.34pt, "100")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(156.33pt, 480.74pt, ". All images were edited with an averaging filter with 4x4-pixel radius. In terms of ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 495.28pt, "time-resolved series, the contrast and brightness remained fixed through the experiment. ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 517.77pt, "The experiments exploring the origin of LC phase contrast and electron scattering were made in the ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 532.07pt, "same imaging mode as previously described. In the desired field of view we performed imaging until ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 546.63pt, "achieving wide region of N phase. The beam was then immediately blanked, moved to the location of ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 561.17pt, "the N phase, and one exposure of STEM diffraction pattern was achieved. The central beam appeared ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 575.71pt, "as diffused disc because of the convergent STEM electron beam. Then imaging continued until the I ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 590.24pt, "phase region appeared in the same area. The beam was then blanked again, moved tens of nanometers ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 604.55pt, "away from the previous position, and STEM diffraction was recorded one more time. The beam position ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 619.11pt, "between two diffraction patterns was shifted slightly to ensure the same impact of any accumulated ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 633.65pt, "layer of contamination products for two images taken adjacent to each other. STEM scans were ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 648.18pt, "performed before, between, and after the diffraction to ensure that the specific phase was present at ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 662.72pt, "the analyzed area based on contrast at the beam location. The exposure time and detector resolution ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 677.03pt, "and binning were adjusted to achieve a reasonable signal level and a stable phase composition at the ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 691.56pt, "beam stop. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12.038pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.887pt, 715.21pt, "Acknowledgements ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
