  #line-at(70.887pt, 336.93pt, "According to the manufacturer, Agar S160 support grids have an amorphous carbon film approximately ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 351.23pt, "28 to 30 nm thick. To be certain, one clean grid was sputtered with gold on both sides using magnetron ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 365.77pt, "sputtering and then cross-sectioned using a focused ion beam (FIB). The cross-section revealed that ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 380.33pt, "the region thinned most by FIB exhibited an artifact in the form of a thickened carbon layer, different ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 394.87pt, "in contrast from the base material (Fig. S4a). Observations of the region less thinned by FIB at the edge ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 409.4pt, "of the lamella confirmed that the carbon film was approximately 25 nm thick (Fig. S4b). Considering ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 423.71pt, "that the carbon grids were subjected to gentle plasma cleaning prior to preparation (which, according ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 438.25pt, "to previous estimates, thins the substrate by approximately 20%), we estimate that the thickness of ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 452.81pt, "the liquid crystal material at the previously measured location ranges from 20 to 40 nm and may be ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 467.34pt, "locally variable, or may even change due to the phase transition of the liquid crystal material. It is also ")
  #line-at(70.887pt, 481.88pt, "possible that in some of the observed locations the sample thickness deviated from our estimate. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.902pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
